<section>
  <p>Mane is built to keep core dictionary search simple and offline-friendly. The app stores learning data on your device so you can keep using saved words, practice history, recent searches, and app settings without creating a separate account.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Stored locally</h2>
  <p>The app may store saved words, learning progress, practice activity, recent search history, and preferences locally on your device. If you sign in with Google, basic account details may also be stored locally so the app can recognize your signed-in state and premium access.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Services we use</h2>
  <p>Premium purchases are processed through Google Play Billing. Ads may be served through Google AdMob. If crash reporting is enabled, Firebase Crashlytics may collect crash and diagnostics data to help improve app stability.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Removing data</h2>
  <p>You can clear local app data, remove saved words, or uninstall the app from your device to delete locally stored information. Mane does not intentionally include searched words or translation text in crash reports.</p>
  <p>Third-party services used by the app operate under their own policies and terms.</p>
</section>
